Hello. Mrs. Anderson.

157
00:11:22.666 --> 00:11:23.833
Elliot's not feeling well.

158
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:25.323
We were just chatting.

159
00:11:26.532 --> 00:11:27.608
It came on all of a sudden.

160
00:11:27.808 --> 00:11:28.916
Probably the heat.

161
00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:34.298
Well. tell him to text me later
if he's feeling better and wants to hang.

162
00:11:34.592 --> 00:11:35.005
I will.

163
00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.833
Tell your mom
that Saturday is perfect.

164
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.083
Of course. Thanks. Mrs. Henderson.

165
00:11:38.333 --> 00:11:38.916
You're welcome. sweetie.

166
00:11:42.166 --> 00:11:43.166
Come on. Sebastian.

167
00:11:43.916 --> 00:11:45.000
Elliot. your dark-haired friend.
is coming down with a baseball bat.

168
00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:48.666
Fuck you.

169
00:11:49.166 --> 00:11:50.416
Give me my bike back.

170
00:11:50.666 --> 00:11:51.416
It's yours?

171
00:11:51.583 --> 00:11:53.083
It's mine now.

172
00:11:53.416 --> 00:11:54.000
Really?

173
00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:55.916
Because if you steal it.
my dad is gonna sue you.

174
00:11:59.083 --> 00:12:00.000
If you've got the balls.
come fight me for it.

175
00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:01.712
But it's already mine.

176
00:12:01.916 --> 00:12:03.716
Jared. what's going on?
Everything okay. honey?

177
00:12:04.595 --> 00:12:05.785
Yeah. we're just messing around.

178
00:12:06.463 --> 00:12:06.876
Yeah.

179
00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:08.756
The bastard in here
is always joking.

180
00:12:09.256 --> 00:12:09.750
Okay.

181
00:12:15.166 --> 00:12:17.250
I can take this whenever I want.

182
00:12:22.916 --> 00:12:24.666
This is gonna be a great summer.

183
00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.500
What do you do? Aren't you bored
going to the beach every day?

184
00:12:43.666 --> 00:12:45.083
Same thing every day.
No. I just...

185
00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.000
I sunbathe.
hang out with my friends.

186
00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:48.000
I'm having a good time.

187
00:12:48.166 --> 00:12:49.083
Skye brought speakers. so...

188
00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.333
She brought Tony Robbins
with you to the beach?

189
00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:56.666
That's exactly what he means.

190
00:12:56.833 --> 00:12:58.083
And James Carville?

191
00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:58.500
Who?

192
00:12:58.700 --> 00:12:59.333
Him?

193
00:12:59.533 --> 00:13:01.166
I just remembered.
The speechwriter.

194
00:13:01.583 --> 00:13:03.000
The one who wrote
Bill Clinton's speeches?

195
00:13:03.583 --> 00:13:04.333
Awesome.

196
00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:06.916
What your father wants to know is...

197
00:13:07.083 --> 00:13:09.000
what's gonna help you
get into an Ivy League school.

198
00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:10.416
Be a lifeguard?

199
00:13:10.583 --> 00:13:11.833
Or do an internship
at a law firm?

200
00:13:11.916 --> 00:13:13.083
With a 4.0 GPA.

201
00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.000
Vacation is for spending time
with my friends.

202
00:13:15.333 --> 00:13:16.416
If you don't have friends.
what's the point?

203
00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:19.500
What your father is trying to say is...

204
00:13:19.583 --> 00:13:21.000
your summer needs a plan.

205
00:13:21.166 --> 00:13:21.916
Some structure.

206
00:13:22.166 --> 00:13:23.083
I have a plan.

207
00:13:23.416 --> 00:13:25.500
I go out. I sleep in.
I tan. and repeat.

208
00:13:25.666 --> 00:13:27.250
Looks like you're already
a lawyer.

209
00:13:27.333 --> 00:13:29.083
No need for law school.
Done.

210
00:13:30.333 --> 00:13:32.803
Just because Grandpa wasn't the first
in the family. doesn't mean
I have to be the first either.

211
00:13:33.003 --> 00:13:34.250
Someone has to break
the family curse.

212
00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:34.754
You know. if Grandpa were alive.

213
00:13:34.954 --> 00:13:35.416
he'd be looking at your hands
and feet before you.

214
00:13:37.416 --> 00:13:38.750
Actually. if Grandpa were alive.
he'd have her locked up
for disobeying her parents.

215
00:13:41.833 --> 00:13:43.833
That's right. I'm tired of
using my brain.

216
00:13:43.916 --> 00:13:45.666
I'm gonna cash in on my hotness
while I'm still young.

217
00:13:45.833 --> 00:13:46.916
Start an OnlyFans.

218
00:13:47.083 --> 00:13:48.000
How do you even know what that is?

219
00:13:48.166 --> 00:13:49.166
Ugh. gross.

220
00:13:49.333 --> 00:13:50.416
Even as a joke.

221
00:13:55.833 --> 00:13:57.715
Why are you playing such an old song?

222
00:13:58.187 --> 00:14:02.500
Mom heard it this morning
and it reminded me of when
you were sweet...

223
00:14:02.666 --> 00:14:03.833
and you were always
all over me.

224
00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.583
That was when I was six.

225
00:14:05.833 --> 00:14:06.916
That's so embarrassing.

226
00:14:07.166 --> 00:14:09.500
It's a mom's job
to embarrass her kids.

227
00:14:09.833 --> 00:14:11.083
You succeeded.

228
00:14:11.916 --> 00:14:13.666
Guys. did you see that weird
ice cream truck?

229
00:14:14.083 --> 00:14:15.166
What's weird about it?
I don't know.

230
00:14:15.333 --> 00:14:18.833
It showed up like it was following me
on purpose. I don't know.

231
00:14:20.916 --> 00:14:22.416
I feel sorry for whoever
kidnaps Jared.

232
00:14:22.583 --> 00:14:23.916
Elizabeth. don't.

233
00:14:24.416 --> 00:14:25.333
Take it back.

234
00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.000
You'd be the perfect kidnap victim.

235
00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:29.166
That's not great either.
but at least it's a positive.

236
00:14:29.333 --> 00:14:30.833
Wait. What's weird about it?

237
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.250
Probably just the music it plays.

238
00:14:33.583 --> 00:14:34.583
I don't know.

239
00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:35.833
It's weird.

240
00:14:36.333 --> 00:14:37.750
Dad didn't see him at the club.

241
00:14:37.916 --> 00:14:38.833
So...

242
00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.250
Mom. are you gonna need
the car tomorrow?

243
00:14:40.583 --> 00:14:41.916
No. probably not. Why?

244
00:14:46.833 --> 00:14:48.583
It's skip day.
Skipping school.

245
00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:49.666
That's what some people call it.

246
00:14:49.833 --> 00:14:51.416
But it's more like a field trip.

247
00:14:51.583 --> 00:14:52.833
That's what everyone calls it.

248
00:14:53.083 --> 00:14:54.500
I heard that Jesse's brother...

249
00:14:54.666 --> 00:14:55.750
is skipping with his friends.

250
00:14:56.083 --> 00:14:57.500
He won't stop talking about it.

251
00:14:57.666 --> 00:14:59.833
I figured we could just go first
and ask for forgiveness later.

252
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.500
Jared. shut up.
That's what makes it so fucking funny. right?

253
00:15:01.666 --> 00:15:03.666
Shut up. It's a tradition
for the juniors...

254
00:15:03.916 --> 00:15:06.000
to spend the last week
with the outgoing seniors.

255
00:15:06.166 --> 00:15:07.833
It's a tradition. It's fun.

256
00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.583
Why didn't we have
that tradition...

257
00:15:13.583 --> 00:15:15.916
So you're telling me that this week
you're all gonna skip school?

258
00:15:16.333 --> 00:15:17.583
Pretty much.

259
00:15:18.333 --> 00:15:19.250
You'll be under
double surveillance.

260
00:15:19.416 --> 00:15:20.500
I'm going. To school.

261
00:15:20.666 --> 00:15:21.500
To the water park.

262
00:15:21.666 --> 00:15:22.916
In your dreams.

263
00:15:23.083 --> 00:15:24.000
Finals are over.

264
00:15:24.083 --> 00:15:25.500
School ends on Wednesday.
No big deal.

265
00:15:25.666 --> 00:15:26.500
Go on Thursday.

266
00:15:26.666 --> 00:15:27.750
Then it's not skipping.

267
00:15:30.083 --> 00:15:31.333
That's exactly the point.
You're supposed to break the rules.

268
00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.916
That's the whole reason
rules exist.

269
00:15:36.166 --> 00:15:37.750
Dad's just playing
the lawyer now. isn't he?

270
00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.333
Dad's defending
the accused.

271
00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:40.666
They didn't do anything wrong.

272
00:15:40.833 --> 00:15:41.916
If they didn't do anything wrong.
then fine.

273
00:15:42.083 --> 00:15:43.500
Honey. mom can give you
the car.

274
00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:44.833
But either way.
you're not going.

275
00:15:50.333 --> 00:15:51.750
Someone has to stay
with Jared.

276
00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.333
No. I can stay.
I can't believe this.

277
00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.333
If something happens.
he can stay at Elliot's.

278
00:15:55.916 --> 00:15:57.250
Which it won't.
Exactly.

279
00:15:57.416 --> 00:15:59.250
As much as we trust
both of you...

280
00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.083
we can't leave
two kids alone.

281
00:16:01.333 --> 00:16:02.750
Accidents can happen.

282
00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:04.333
We want an adult
to be there.

283
00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.916
And in this case.
that adult is you. Okay?

284
00:16:07.083 --> 00:16:07.916
Either way...

285
00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:09.416
you have to go to skip day.

286
00:16:10.666 --> 00:16:11.916
Find someone to stay with you.

287
00:16:12.083 --> 00:16:13.166
Otherwise I'm taking you with me.

288
00:16:13.333 --> 00:16:15.750
No. don't take me to the water park.

289
00:16:15.916 --> 00:16:17.416
It's full of girls in bikinis.

290
00:16:17.666 --> 00:16:18.166
Shut up. Jared.

291
00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:21.416
It's no place for a pre-teen like me.
You're so annoying.

292
00:16:21.583 --> 00:16:23.166
You're not taking me either.
Yeah.

293
00:16:23.333 --> 00:16:24.250
Take you where?

294
00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.166
I'll take you to school tomorrow.

295
00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.916
I'd love to see Dad
go to school

296
00:16:28.083 --> 00:16:29.666
and talk about Mitt Romney.

297
00:16:31.333 --> 00:16:32.666
Mitt Romney.

298
00:16:32.833 --> 00:16:33.666
Why. sweetie?

299
00:16:33.833 --> 00:16:35.833
Do we have Mitt Romney
for dessert. ice cream?

300
00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:52.666
Piper.

301
00:17:56.083 --> 00:17:57.166
Honey. what's wrong?

302
00:17:58.416 --> 00:18:00.000
Do you have more ice cream?

303
00:18:17.166 --> 00:18:18.166
Fran!

304
00:18:18.583 --> 00:18:19.833
What's going on?

305
00:18:20.916 --> 00:18:21.916
Fran!

306
00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:28.916
Oh my God!

307
00:18:30.166 --> 00:18:31.250
Oh my God!

308
00:18:32.416 --> 00:18:33.750
Brett!

309
00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:13.500
Watch out. kids.

310
00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:19.416
Sweetie. what's wrong?

311
00:19:19.583 --> 00:19:20.416
My necklace.

312
00:19:20.583 --> 00:19:21.666
I dropped it.

313
00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:23.666
We'll find it tomorrow.

314
00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:24.750
Go to bed.

315
00:19:24.833 --> 00:19:26.333
But I can't sleep
without it.

316
00:19:26.416 --> 00:19:27.416
Please. Daddy.

317
00:19:28.583 --> 00:19:29.416
Okay.

318
00:19:32.166 --> 00:19:33.750
Okay.

319
00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:36.916
Sweetie.

320
00:19:37.666 --> 00:19:38.666
Are you sure?

321
00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:41.500
I don't see anything.

322
00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.583
What's that?

323
00:19:51.916 --> 00:19:53.750
Is that oil?

324
00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:55.250
Sebastian?

325
00:19:55.416 --> 00:19:57.250
Our kids have completely
lost their minds.

326
00:20:16.333 --> 00:20:17.333
Steve.

327
00:20:18.833 --> 00:20:19.833
Honey.

328
00:20:20.666 --> 00:20:21.666
I have a gun.

329
00:20:22.166 --> 00:20:23.166
I'll shoot.

330
00:20:33.083 --> 00:20:34.000
Elliot!

331
00:20:34.583 --> 00:20:35.833
Honey. what are you doing?

332
00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.500
What did you do to Dad?

333
00:20:40.333 --> 00:20:41.916
Fuck. what is that?

334
00:20:42.083 --> 00:20:43.000
Elliot!

335
00:20:43.166 --> 00:20:45.083
What are you doing?

336
00:20:49.166 --> 00:20:50.500
Elliot. put it down.

337
00:20:51.083 --> 00:20:52.000
Elliot!

338
00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:55.666
Elliot!

339
00:20:56.333 --> 00:20:57.500
Enough. come to Mom.

340
00:20:57.750 --> 00:20:59.500
Come to Mom right now.

341
00:20:59.916 --> 00:21:00.750
No!

342
00:21:00.833 --> 00:21:01.833
What are you doing?

343
00:21:02.583 --> 00:21:03.416
Put it down.

344
00:21:03.583 --> 00:21:05.916
No. no. no. honey!

345
00:21:06.083 --> 00:21:07.416
No. don't do it!

346
00:21:07.583 --> 00:21:08.416
No. no. no!

347
00:21:08.666 --> 00:21:09.666
Come to Mom. please.

348
00:21:10.666 --> 00:21:11.750
Mom loves you.

349
00:21:11.916 --> 00:21:13.333
No! No!

350
00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:27.083
Come here. sweetie. Come on.

351
00:22:28.250 --> 00:22:29.916
Good job. baby.

352
00:22:31.333 --> 00:22:32.500
Oh my God!

353
00:22:34.166 --> 00:22:34.750
Are you okay?

354
00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:36.500
What happened?

355
00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:38.916
Someone hurt my mom.

356
00:22:39.431 --> 00:22:40.087
Who?

357
00:22:41.167 --> 00:22:42.219
Me.

358
00:22:47.750 --> 00:22:48.583
What's going on?

359
00:22:48.916 --> 00:22:50.416
The Farbers left
the door open.

360
00:22:51.416 --> 00:22:52.666
Probably getting ready to leave.

361
00:22:53.500 --> 00:22:54.416
Should I go close it?

362
00:22:54.833 --> 00:22:56.083
No. they'll figure it out.

363
00:22:56.750 --> 00:22:58.583
Better text Fran
just in case.

364
00:23:00.333 --> 00:23:01.166
What?

365
00:23:01.333 --> 00:23:01.750
Why is there
an ice cream truck here?

366
00:23:06.333 --> 00:23:07.833
I heard Lizzie and Skye
making a big fuss.

367
00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:10.333
After they found out
they're not going to skip day.

368
00:23:11.916 --> 00:23:13.416
That guy gives me
the creeps.

369
00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:15.916
Damn it.

370
00:23:16.833 --> 00:23:18.750
I thought we were doing
ice cream puns.

371
00:23:20.916 --> 00:23:22.166
Which is a little weird.

372
00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:25.083
Probably nothing.

373
00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:28.000
I'll call security
to come take a look.

374
00:23:47.506 --> 00:23:48.405
Watch out.

375
00:24:12.083 --> 00:24:15.500
Your mom left this here.

376
00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:23.583
Muk.

377
00:24:29.500 --> 00:24:30.416
Brett.

378
00:24:36.250 --> 00:24:37.416
You're sick. aren't you?

379
00:24:38.416 --> 00:24:41.583
See you at school. I guess.

380
00:24:44.416 --> 00:24:45.416
She's acting really weird.

381
00:25:38.166 --> 00:25:39.333
What the hell...

382
00:25:50.500 --> 00:25:51.250
Elliot. Elliot!

383
00:25:54.916 --> 00:25:55.833
Damn it.

384
00:25:57.333 --> 00:25:58.916
Oh my God. Marcella!

385
00:25:59.681 --> 00:26:00.812
So. I edited the video.

386
00:26:01.012 --> 00:26:02.885
and I thought we could
do a little...

387
00:26:04.853 --> 00:26:06.387
Okay.

388
00:26:22.750 --> 00:26:26.333
What's this? Are we having a contest
for who can dress like a zombie in pajamas?

389
00:26:29.500 --> 00:26:30.833
Good morning. Mr. Mayfer.

390
00:26:31.083 --> 00:26:33.000
Any sign of your friend
Mr. Henderson?

391
00:26:33.916 --> 00:26:35.416
I saw him a little while ago.

392
00:26:35.583 --> 00:26:36.333
He's a mess.

393
00:26:36.500 --> 00:26:38.666
He said he was going
to the nurse's office.

394
00:26:39.166 --> 00:26:39.416
Yeah.

395
00:26:39.750 --> 00:26:41.864
The terrible illness
called summer.

396
00:26:42.416 --> 00:26:43.000
It strikes around the end
of every school year.

397
00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:50.333
Want me to go check?

398
00:26:50.833 --> 00:26:52.083
Yes. but come back quick.

399
00:26:52.250 --> 00:26:53.833
Because there's only
a few days left.

400
00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:56.666
So we still have
three days of school.

401
00:26:57.833 --> 00:27:00.166
Let's continue
with fractions and mixed numbers.

402
00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:04.333
Who can break down
72 into prime factors?

403
00:27:14.083 --> 00:27:15.666
Are you okay?

404
00:27:17.083 --> 00:27:18.333
Stop asking me that.

405
00:27:18.833 --> 00:27:19.750
How does it look to you?

406
00:27:20.833 --> 00:27:21.250
Sorry. I just...

407
00:27:23.083 --> 00:27:25.583
Is it just me or is something
weird going on?

408
00:27:27.166 --> 00:27:30.265
You shouldn't be skipping class.
It's my responsibility.

409
00:27:33.666 --> 00:27:35.617
Everything's normal.
Yeah.

410
00:27:36.397 --> 00:27:37.619
For Tommy.

411
00:27:43.262 --> 00:27:43.985
Elliot?

412
00:27:46.188 --> 00:27:47.448
Did you see Elliot?

413
00:27:48.904 --> 00:27:50.105
Guys.

414
00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:54.416
I thought someone was outside.

415
00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:29.666
Do we have a test today or what?

416
00:28:32.166 --> 00:28:33.160
Mr. B. you can't give us
a test

417
00:28:33.360 --> 00:28:34.333
on the last week
of school.

418
00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:37.500
At least now I know
it's not a joke.

419
00:28:37.916 --> 00:28:38.750
What joke?

420
00:28:38.916 --> 00:28:39.833
Ask your friends.

421
00:28:40.559 --> 00:28:43.693
Someone told them it's silent day
or some new holiday they invented.

422
00:28:45.166 --> 00:28:46.083
Hey. guys!

423
00:28:49.351 --> 00:28:50.250
Greg is sick
and won't talk.

424
00:28:50.904 --> 00:28:52.318
Watch your language. Mr. Green.

425
00:28:53.110 --> 00:28:53.232
Language.

426
00:28:53.638 --> 00:28:55.750
I'm the only one talking.
Don't you think that's weird?

427
00:28:56.500 --> 00:28:59.000
I thought everyone had left
for vacation.

428
00:28:59.416 --> 00:29:00.666
But since you're here...

429
00:29:01.250 --> 00:29:02.500
take out the microscope.

430
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:07.000
What do you mean she didn't show up?

431
00:29:07.166 --> 00:29:07.916
Mr. Hamlin...

432
00:29:08.083 --> 00:29:09.083
Should we go check her house?

433
00:29:09.250 --> 00:29:10.166
Mr. Hamlin!

434
00:29:12.886 --> 00:29:15.542
You don't understand.

435
00:29:40.500 --> 00:29:41.083
Sorry.

436
00:29:41.583 --> 00:29:42.333
What are you doing?

437
00:29:43.333 --> 00:29:44.250
Sorry.

438
00:29:45.166 --> 00:29:45.916
Hello?

439
00:29:46.166 --> 00:29:47.916
Class isn't over yet.

440
00:29:48.416 --> 00:29:49.083
I don't know.

441
00:30:08.583 --> 00:30:08.916
Sorry.

442
00:30:09.500 --> 00:30:10.250
Where are you going?

443
00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:12.166
Are you skipping?

444
00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:14.333
Sorry. no. Where are you going?

445
00:30:14.583 --> 00:30:15.833
No. class
isn't over yet.

446
00:30:16.083 --> 00:30:18.416
Tommy. get back here right now!
Okay. okay.

447
00:30:20.833 --> 00:30:22.583
I'll deal with Tommy
and the others later.

448
00:30:22.833 --> 00:30:25.343
Now. all of you.
back to your seats.

449
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:28.583
Sit down.

450
00:30:29.539 --> 00:30:32.500
Marcella.

451
00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:33.833
Elliot.

452
00:30:34.083 --> 00:30:35.000
Elliot. this isn't funny.

453
00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:44.250
Frank. what's going on?

454
00:30:44.416 --> 00:30:46.416
The whole school is filled
with ice cream fudge.

455
00:30:46.666 --> 00:30:47.416
Ready? Let's go.

456
00:30:48.583 --> 00:30:49.583
Ice cream break!

457
00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:51.333
This is not a fire drill!

458
00:30:52.416 --> 00:30:53.416
Back to class. now!

459
00:30:56.500 --> 00:30:57.750
What the hell is going on here?

460
00:30:58.500 --> 00:30:59.333
Must be a prank.

461
00:31:00.083 --> 00:31:01.250
There's gotta be
a camera somewhere.

462
00:31:01.666 --> 00:31:02.666
We know you're filming us.

463
00:31:02.866 --> 00:31:03.866
Yeah.

464
00:31:15.250 --> 00:31:16.000
Elliot!

465
00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:17.833
Come on.

466
00:31:19.083 --> 00:31:19.872
Elliot. please!

467
00:31:20.072 --> 00:31:20.333
Elliot. don't think about it

468
00:31:20.971 --> 00:31:21.753
Get out.

469
00:31:35.083 --> 00:31:35.833
Jared!

470
00:31:38.750 --> 00:31:39.416
The smell...

471
00:31:39.916 --> 00:31:40.583
Cover your nose.

472
00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:46.250
Move aside.
I want to get through.

473
00:31:46.583 --> 00:31:47.750
Show some respect.

474
00:31:49.833 --> 00:31:50.250
What flavor is it?

475
00:31:52.250 --> 00:31:53.583
That much?

476
00:31:53.750 --> 00:31:54.916
Give yours to me.

477
00:31:56.750 --> 00:31:58.750
Okay. fine.

478
00:32:11.002 --> 00:32:11.555
No.

479
00:32:12.250 --> 00:32:14.166
Oh my God! Oh my God!

480
00:32:15.500 --> 00:32:15.833
Kids. don't look!

481
00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:19.166
Someone get a doctor!

482
00:32:30.750 --> 00:32:31.083
Don't laugh...

483
00:32:35.250 --> 00:32:37.583
It's not funny at all.
Damn it!

484
00:32:51.250 --> 00:32:52.500
What the hell is going on?

485
00:32:52.666 --> 00:32:54.166
Back off! That's enough!
I said back off!

486
00:32:58.333 --> 00:32:58.916
Oh my God!

487
00:33:02.166 --> 00:33:03.583
My boy... Oh my God!

488
00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:05.250
911. how can I help you?

489
00:33:06.166 --> 00:33:06.416
Yes. sir.

490
00:33:06.583 --> 00:33:08.083
My name is Bob Maloney.
from Meadowbrook.

491
00:33:08.333 --> 00:33:08.732
Please come quickly!

492
00:33:08.932 --> 00:33:12.548
I'm not sure if the kid jumped
or if it was an accident. but it looks like...

493
00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:14.250
Yes. sir.

494
00:33:30.833 --> 00:33:31.416
And then there was a brick...

495
00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:45.750
What?

496
00:34:16.382 --> 00:34:17.980
Damn it. the bike is lost.

497
00:34:23.665 --> 00:34:25.160
What happened here?

498
00:34:27.333 --> 00:34:28.000
What's going on? Come in!

499
00:34:29.769 --> 00:34:30.783
Oh my God.

500
00:34:50.750 --> 00:34:53.250
Now let's look at
the housefly.

501
00:34:53.416 --> 00:34:56.250
It might seem like
a completely ordinary insect.

502
00:34:56.666 --> 00:34:59.083
but if you look at it closely.

503
00:34:59.250 --> 00:35:01.583
you'll see that it has
the same characteristics.

504
00:35:14.500 --> 00:35:15.083
Let's go find ours.

505
00:35:15.283 --> 00:35:17.277
This room is usually
always quiet

506
00:35:21.750 --> 00:35:23.000
What are you doing?

507
00:35:23.166 --> 00:35:24.000
Let me go!

508
00:35:24.166 --> 00:35:25.250
What are you gonna do to me?

509
00:35:25.916 --> 00:35:26.500
Let me go!

510
00:35:28.333 --> 00:35:29.083
Get in.

511
00:35:30.333 --> 00:35:30.666
No way!

512
00:35:31.416 --> 00:35:31.666
Oh my God!

513
00:35:54.750 --> 00:35:56.759
Is this really happening?
I know.

514
00:35:56.959 --> 00:35:57.959
What the hell?

515
00:36:43.750 --> 00:36:44.583
Oh my God!

516
00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:53.416
Okay. Manny.

517
00:37:05.416 --> 00:37:06.333
Come on. hurry up!

518
00:37:10.500 --> 00:37:11.416
Marcella!

519
00:37:11.500 --> 00:37:12.416
Come here!

520
00:37:20.833 --> 00:37:22.166
Mia. it's me.

521
00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:24.750
Where's Tommy?
He's at the back exit.

522
00:37:29.666 --> 00:37:31.166
Help! Help!

523
00:37:37.583 --> 00:37:38.666
What's that?
What the hell is that?

524
00:37:45.583 --> 00:37:46.166
Sting! Let's go!

525
00:37:52.916 --> 00:37:53.250
Here! Come here!

526
00:37:54.416 --> 00:37:57.416
Here! Come on. come on!
Tommy. get in! Close the door!

527
00:38:04.666 --> 00:38:06.250
What the hell is going on?

528
00:38:06.750 --> 00:38:07.583
Something bad.

529
00:38:07.833 --> 00:38:09.416
Someone bad.

530
00:38:09.916 --> 00:38:10.833
The ice cream man.

531
00:38:11.916 --> 00:38:12.916
The police are coming!

532
00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:17.250
Back off!

533
00:38:18.416 --> 00:38:21.250
Back off. kids!
I need everyone to back off. please.

534
00:38:24.083 --> 00:38:25.250
Back! Hurry. back!

535
00:38:42.018 --> 00:38:42.912
Oh my God.

536
00:38:44.250 --> 00:38:44.583
What are you doing?

537
00:38:51.916 --> 00:38:55.916
Ring-a-ding-ding...
That's the ice cream man's song.

538
00:38:57.666 --> 00:38:58.583
Why are you singing?

539
00:38:58.833 --> 00:38:59.833
Stop singing. now!
Stop it right now!

540
00:39:01.416 --> 00:39:01.916
It's not funny.

541
00:39:05.166 --> 00:39:06.166
Shit!

542
00:39:06.333 --> 00:39:07.666
They threw glue in his face!

543
00:39:08.333 --> 00:39:09.166
We need to find a phone.

544
00:39:09.583 --> 00:39:11.000
Hold on. I've got one.

545
00:39:17.250 --> 00:39:18.666
What? That's the top model!

546
00:39:18.916 --> 00:39:20.333
It's like an iPhone.

547
00:39:20.583 --> 00:39:21.750
You know more people
use Android.

548
00:39:21.916 --> 00:39:22.833
Just make the call!

549
00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:25.253
- We didn't say anything
- Yeah. talk to yourself

550
00:39:25.653 --> 00:39:26.083
I'm watching you
out of the corner of my eye.

551
00:39:26.916 --> 00:39:29.416
This is the number
for Martin Mayfer's office.

552
00:39:29.750 --> 00:39:30.500
Leave a message.

553
00:39:30.833 --> 00:39:32.000
I'll try calling Mom.

554
00:39:34.333 --> 00:39:36.083
Sorry. how does this work?

555
00:39:36.500 --> 00:39:38.166
Shit!
The fire department is here.

556
00:39:39.583 --> 00:39:39.833
Where is it? Where are you?

557
00:39:40.033 --> 00:39:40.166
Here! Help us!

558
00:39:40.666 --> 00:39:41.583
Look over there!

559
00:39:42.750 --> 00:39:45.499
Don't come closer. kid!
Back off.

560
00:39:46.018 --> 00:39:47.256
Hang in there.

561
00:39:54.416 --> 00:39:55.333
I'm here.

562
00:39:56.250 --> 00:39:57.000
Step back.

563
00:40:04.916 --> 00:40:06.583
Hey. hey.

564
00:40:07.166 --> 00:40:08.000
No. wait!

565
00:40:47.166 --> 00:40:48.083
He's here.

566
00:40:48.916 --> 00:40:49.333
Everyone. follow him.

567
00:40:50.916 --> 00:40:51.750
We need to move fast.

568
00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:54.833
I don't know. but we can't
stay here.

569
00:40:58.500 --> 00:40:59.666
Oh my God!

570
00:41:13.333 --> 00:41:15.000
They don't want to kill us.

571
00:41:16.166 --> 00:41:17.333
They want to take us...

572
00:41:17.916 --> 00:41:18.833
Oh my God!

573
00:41:20.000 --> 00:41:20.916
Is this for real?

574
00:41:21.333 --> 00:41:22.000
What's that sound?

575
00:41:27.333 --> 00:41:27.750
What the hell?

576
00:41:27.916 --> 00:41:28.333
What's that?

577
00:41:33.666 --> 00:41:34.666
Damn it!

578
00:41:35.583 --> 00:41:36.916
What the hell is that?

579
00:41:39.333 --> 00:41:40.916
The ice cream is possessed!

580
00:41:41.333 --> 00:41:42.166
Did you eat it?

581
00:41:42.500 --> 00:41:44.166
What? No. I'm lactose intolerant.

582
00:41:44.333 --> 00:41:45.833
Probably more than
you want to know. but...

583
00:41:46.000 --> 00:41:47.000
Hold on. sorry.

584
00:41:47.416 --> 00:41:48.750
What do you mean possessed?

585
00:41:48.916 --> 00:41:49.750
It turns you into a demon.

586
00:41:49.950 --> 00:41:50.166
Did you eat it?

587
00:41:50.366 --> 00:41:50.750
Did you eat it or not?

588
00:41:51.000 --> 00:41:52.000
I threw it up. I'm fine.

589
00:41:52.166 --> 00:41:53.333
So can we trust her?

590
00:41:53.750 --> 00:41:55.844
I saw her throw up.
Okay.

591
00:41:56.644 --> 00:41:58.123
Hold on.
Were you watching me?

592
00:41:58.416 --> 00:42:00.000
No. no... Okay. yes. a little.

593
00:42:00.500 --> 00:42:01.916
But not in a creepy way.

594
00:42:02.333 --> 00:42:04.333
I just happened to see you.

595
00:42:04.500 --> 00:42:05.583
Jared. it's okay.

596
00:42:05.666 --> 00:42:07.166
I got it all out.

597
00:42:07.833 --> 00:42:09.500
Okay. I'll keep an eye on you.

598
00:42:09.750 --> 00:42:10.333
Okay. what do you say?

599
00:42:10.666 --> 00:42:13.416
Help us figure out a way
out of here.

600
00:42:13.583 --> 00:42:14.750
Hold on. Lizzie.

601
00:42:46.166 --> 00:42:47.833
Help! Someone. help me!

602
00:42:49.000 --> 00:42:49.750
What the hell is going on?

603
00:42:51.250 --> 00:42:52.166
Siri!

604
00:42:52.583 --> 00:42:54.000
Call Mom and Dad.

605
00:42:58.583 --> 00:43:00.333
This is Martin Mayfer's office.

606
00:43:00.500 --> 00:43:02.000
Leave a message
and we'll get back to you.

607
00:43:05.166 --> 00:43:06.083
Siri!

608
00:43:06.666 --> 00:43:09.250
Call that idiot!
Turn off the sound. man!

609
00:43:13.250 --> 00:43:13.833
Shut up. it's Lizzie.

610
00:43:14.750 --> 00:43:16.083
Lizzie. I'm losing my mind!

611
00:43:16.250 --> 00:43:17.583
The kids are killing everyone!

612
00:43:17.833 --> 00:43:20.333
You need to get here. now!
I can't move my arm at all.

613
00:43:20.666 --> 00:43:21.583
Call an ambulance!

614
00:43:21.916 --> 00:43:23.416
What? Call
Mom or Dad.

615
00:43:23.750 --> 00:43:25.000
No. let's call a doctor.

616
00:43:25.083 --> 00:43:26.583
I already tried calling them.
but I got voicemail.

617
00:43:26.750 --> 00:43:28.416
Wait. did you have ice cream?

618
00:43:28.583 --> 00:43:29.500
What?

619
00:43:29.750 --> 00:43:31.416
Last night.
Skye and I had some.

620
00:43:31.500 --> 00:43:33.333
Jared. this is an emergency!

621
00:43:33.500 --> 00:43:34.083
It's poisoned.

622
00:43:34.666 --> 00:43:35.416
It's possessed.

623
00:43:35.666 --> 00:43:36.333
You need to get it out
of your system.

624
00:43:36.533 --> 00:43:37.166
You need to throw up.

625
00:43:37.333 --> 00:43:39.083
I told you I can't
move my arms!

626
00:43:39.250 --> 00:43:40.666
I'm paralyzed
all over my body.

627
00:43:40.833 --> 00:43:42.333
It might cause
paralysis in teenagers.

628
00:43:42.500 --> 00:43:43.583
Or it could make them
pass out.

629
00:43:43.833 --> 00:43:45.083
You need to throw up.

630
00:43:45.250 --> 00:43:46.583
I said use a toothbrush.

631
00:43:46.916 --> 00:43:49.083
I heard her.

632
00:43:51.083 --> 00:43:52.083
Jared.

633
00:43:52.583 --> 00:43:53.750
You need to get out of there.

634
00:43:53.916 --> 00:43:56.317
I know. We're praying
they don't find us.

635
00:43:56.517 --> 00:43:58.034
If we go to church...

636
00:43:59.916 --> 00:44:01.333
The demonic creature
can't go in there.

637
00:44:01.666 --> 00:44:02.666
To the church.

638
00:44:02.916 --> 00:44:04.166
No one's ever gone down
to the basement.

639
00:44:04.333 --> 00:44:06.000
If you can get there.
I can come pick you up.

640
00:44:07.833 --> 00:44:08.500
The church.

641
00:44:18.583 --> 00:44:19.500
Shit!

642
00:44:30.333 --> 00:44:31.166
We're screwed.
Let's go. let's go!

643
00:44:31.416 --> 00:44:32.416
Let's go!

644
00:45:47.833 --> 00:45:50.083
Don't be a chicken. do it!

645
00:45:50.583 --> 00:45:51.416
Do it!

646
00:45:51.666 --> 00:45:52.666
You can do it!

647
00:45:54.500 --> 00:45:55.500
Damn it!

648
00:46:17.833 --> 00:46:19.333
Get away from there.

649
00:46:33.583 --> 00:46:34.750
What the hell is that?

650
00:46:35.333 --> 00:46:37.000
Tell them to be quiet.

651
00:46:51.500 --> 00:46:52.416
Hello?

652
00:46:55.000 --> 00:46:55.916
Mrs. Poole?

653
00:47:08.583 --> 00:47:08.916
Penelope. what are you doing?

654
00:47:12.250 --> 00:47:13.666
We need to get out of here.
Come on.

655
00:47:17.250 --> 00:47:17.833
Penelope!

656
00:47:50.250 --> 00:47:51.916
Skye. Skye!

657
00:47:53.833 --> 00:47:54.416
Skye. wake up. hurry!

658
00:48:57.666 --> 00:48:59.166
I knew you'd understand.

659
00:49:10.666 --> 00:49:12.000
New phone? Who is it?

660
00:49:12.416 --> 00:49:13.750
Chris. stop messing around.

661
00:49:13.916 --> 00:49:15.166
Help us.
The kids have gone crazy.

662
00:49:15.333 --> 00:49:16.583
They attacked people.

663
00:49:17.333 --> 00:49:18.666
What are you talking about?

664
00:49:30.250 --> 00:49:31.000
Shit!

665
00:49:37.916 --> 00:49:38.666
Wen. this way!

666
00:49:38.916 --> 00:49:40.166
It can get in now!

667
00:49:43.000 --> 00:49:44.000
Try that.

668
00:49:44.500 --> 00:49:46.083
Yeah. use it! Yes. yes!

669
00:49:46.333 --> 00:49:48.000
Why is it so heavy?

670
00:49:48.166 --> 00:49:49.166
Spray them!

671
00:49:49.416 --> 00:49:49.666
Hurry!

672
00:49:50.500 --> 00:49:51.416
First. take out the pin.

673
00:49:51.666 --> 00:49:52.583
Take out the pin!

674
00:49:52.833 --> 00:49:53.500
What are you doing?

675
00:49:53.750 --> 00:49:55.083
Hurry. take out the pin!

676
00:49:55.250 --> 00:49:56.500
Want me to help you?

677
00:49:57.750 --> 00:49:58.166
Okay.

678
00:49:58.333 --> 00:50:00.500
Now that it's ready.
spray them!

679
00:50:03.583 --> 00:50:04.666
Let's go!

680
00:50:06.916 --> 00:50:07.916
Oh my God!

681
00:50:08.083 --> 00:50:09.166
We did it!

682
00:50:10.666 --> 00:50:12.000
Let's go. let's go!

683
00:50:31.583 --> 00:50:32.583
Get inside. quick!

684
00:50:33.333 --> 00:50:35.083
Damn it. it's locked!
What are you doing?

685
00:50:35.250 --> 00:50:36.083
I'm trying!

686
00:50:36.250 --> 00:50:37.166
The door is locked!

687
00:50:37.416 --> 00:50:38.250
Jessie! Jessie!

688
00:50:43.083 --> 00:50:43.750
We can't make it! Let's go!

689
00:50:45.833 --> 00:50:46.666
Hurry. let's go!

690
00:50:47.250 --> 00:50:47.916
Break it!

691
00:50:50.583 --> 00:50:51.833
Damn it! I'm losing my mind!

692
00:50:57.666 --> 00:50:58.500
Damn it!

693
00:50:59.416 --> 00:51:00.333
Everyone!

694
00:51:00.583 --> 00:51:02.000
What's that?

695
00:51:03.333 --> 00:51:04.333
Close the door. quick!

696
00:51:06.500 --> 00:51:07.833
I'll lock the door.

697
00:51:13.416 --> 00:51:14.416
We're trapped.

698
00:51:16.333 --> 00:51:16.833
The outside door.

699
00:51:17.166 --> 00:51:18.666
There! There's one there too.

700
00:51:24.833 --> 00:51:25.166
Go. go. go.

701
00:51:43.916 --> 00:51:44.416
We won't leave
anyone behind.

702
00:51:46.166 --> 00:51:46.583
We won't...

703
00:51:50.666 --> 00:51:53.250
The other side of the fence
leads to the church.

704
00:51:57.333 --> 00:51:57.833
We just need to get
to that patrol car.

705
00:52:11.000 --> 00:52:11.666
Damn it. Jared. hurry!

706
00:52:15.750 --> 00:52:16.916
Forget it. it's okay.
Come on. hurry!

707
00:52:17.083 --> 00:52:18.000
What are you waiting for?

708
00:52:18.166 --> 00:52:19.500
Take it. I don't want it back.

709
00:52:20.000 --> 00:52:21.250
Oh my God...

710
00:52:21.450 --> 00:52:23.423
What's that?

711
00:52:25.333 --> 00:52:26.916
Hurry. they'll kill us.

712
00:52:29.273 --> 00:52:30.086
What a mess.

713
00:52:30.833 --> 00:52:31.500
Come on!

714
00:52:35.416 --> 00:52:37.083
I'm telling you. I'm a genius.

715
00:52:37.250 --> 00:52:38.333
This hand is like magic.

716
00:52:39.477 --> 00:52:39.830
No.

717
00:52:40.030 --> 00:52:40.416
I'm not...

718
00:52:40.616 --> 00:52:40.833
Good. right?

719
00:52:41.833 --> 00:52:42.583
Don't look back.

720
00:52:43.666 --> 00:52:43.916
Run. hurry!

721
00:52:46.333 --> 00:52:46.833
Sorry.

722
00:52:54.250 --> 00:52:55.333
What the hell is that?

723
00:52:56.333 --> 00:52:57.166
I'm losing my mind.

724
00:52:57.333 --> 00:52:58.333
Keep going. let's go!

725
00:53:28.416 --> 00:53:29.701
Okay. that way.
Wait for them to leave first.

726
00:53:29.901 --> 00:53:31.500
But there's too many.
But it's the shortest way.

727
00:53:33.833 --> 00:53:35.166
I don't know... it looks
like suicide.

728
00:53:35.416 --> 00:53:36.333
Better find
another way.

729
00:53:36.583 --> 00:53:38.166
We absolutely have
to get to the church.

730
00:53:38.666 --> 00:53:39.750
Mia! Oh my God!

731
00:53:41.083 --> 00:53:42.250
Sebastian. are you okay?

732
00:53:42.500 --> 00:53:42.833
I'm fine.

733
00:53:43.583 --> 00:53:44.750
Mia. are you okay?

734
00:53:53.583 --> 00:53:54.416
Thanks. No problem.

735
00:53:54.666 --> 00:53:55.666
How did you know to do that?

736
00:53:55.916 --> 00:53:56.916
I'm twelve years old.

737
00:53:57.083 --> 00:53:58.000
I already know how to make
myself throw up.

738
00:53:58.666 --> 00:54:00.083
That's dark. I like it.

739
00:54:00.333 --> 00:54:01.416
We need to get to the church.

740
00:54:02.916 --> 00:54:03.250
Let's go. let's go.

741
00:54:18.416 --> 00:54:19.166
I'm losing it.

742
00:54:19.750 --> 00:54:20.250
What the hell?

743
00:54:29.083 --> 00:54:29.812
Pass the rope. pass it.

744
00:54:30.012 --> 00:54:31.833
One single rope. weave it tight.
Hold on tight. don't let go.

745
00:54:35.000 --> 00:54:35.583
Let's go. let's go.

746
00:54:40.333 --> 00:54:40.833
Get up. hurry.

747
00:54:41.083 --> 00:54:42.416
I'm stuck!

748
00:54:50.583 --> 00:54:52.250
Hurry. hurry!

749
00:54:53.916 --> 00:54:54.833
Don't let it
take over me.

750
00:54:57.583 --> 00:54:58.416
Idiot!

751
00:54:59.333 --> 00:55:00.166
I'll beat you black and blue!

752
00:55:02.166 --> 00:55:03.416
Run! Run!

753
00:55:11.250 --> 00:55:12.583
Hey. you useless piece of shit!

754
00:55:37.166 --> 00:55:38.083
This way!

755
00:56:00.666 --> 00:56:01.000
Okay.

756
00:56:19.333 --> 00:56:20.250
Guys...

757
00:56:21.333 --> 00:56:22.250
What?

758
00:56:24.666 --> 00:56:26.500
Why does the church
have a freezer like that?

759
00:56:26.666 --> 00:56:28.250
Probably where they keep
the bodies.

760
00:56:28.583 --> 00:56:29.416
What bodies?

761
00:56:29.583 --> 00:56:30.500
For funerals.

762
00:56:32.500 --> 00:56:33.416
The ice cream...

763
00:56:34.000 --> 00:56:34.916
It's in there.

764
00:56:35.333 --> 00:56:36.416
Not in the truck?

765
00:56:36.916 --> 00:56:38.416
Maybe they have
a bigger plan.

766
00:56:48.666 --> 00:56:49.666
There it is!

767
00:56:56.833 --> 00:56:57.833
Oh hell.

768
00:57:05.833 --> 00:57:09.666
Damn it! They're all in here.

769
00:57:10.166 --> 00:57:11.083
I told you.

770
00:57:11.250 --> 00:57:12.333
Let's defrost it.

771
00:57:14.166 --> 00:57:15.916
Find the plug or the switch.

772
00:57:29.500 --> 00:57:30.500
Oh my God!

773
00:57:30.666 --> 00:57:31.916
Yes. oh my God!

774
00:57:32.333 --> 00:57:33.750
The switch is right next to him.

775
00:57:40.750 --> 00:57:42.833
Save yourselves!

776
00:57:43.250 --> 00:57:44.750
Leave!
He's telling us to leave!

777
00:57:44.916 --> 00:57:46.416
No way.
the ice cream man is there!

778
00:57:46.583 --> 00:57:47.666
The door!

779
00:57:48.666 --> 00:57:50.000
Damn it. no!

780
00:57:52.500 --> 00:57:54.500
We're screwed.
We're gonna die in here.

781
00:57:56.666 --> 00:57:57.666
At least
we're going to Heaven.

782
00:57:57.916 --> 00:57:59.916
Tommy. your joke
is not helping.

783
00:58:00.500 --> 00:58:01.416
I wasn't joking.

784
00:58:01.500 --> 00:58:02.333
There's no signal at all.

785
00:58:02.500 --> 00:58:04.386
But Lizzie said
she's coming here. so...

786
00:58:04.586 --> 00:58:05.750
Good thing we're
in the freezer.

787
00:58:05.916 --> 00:58:08.416
That's the first place
everyone will look. Jared.

788
00:58:12.916 --> 00:58:13.916
Want me to get you down?

789
00:58:14.416 --> 00:58:15.000
Chris.

790
00:58:15.250 --> 00:58:16.333
Help me down.

791
00:58:16.666 --> 00:58:18.333
So now you finally agree
to be with me?

792
00:58:19.083 --> 00:58:20.750
Very funny.
Get me down. hurry.

793
00:58:21.166 --> 00:58:22.750
First promise me
you won't be a dick.

794
00:58:23.416 --> 00:58:25.166
Seriously?
We're gonna do this now?

795
00:58:27.666 --> 00:58:28.250
No better time.

796
00:58:30.750 --> 00:58:31.833
Okay. Chris. I...

797
00:58:32.916 --> 00:58:34.416
I promise I won't do
anything stupid.

798
00:58:34.916 --> 00:58:36.083
And if you help me down.

799
00:58:36.333 --> 00:58:38.333
I might consider going
to dinner with you.

800
00:58:38.583 --> 00:58:40.166
Assuming there's
any restaurant left.

801
00:58:40.333 --> 00:58:42.166
But first. can you
help me get down?

802
00:58:44.666 --> 00:58:45.833
Dinner or a movie?

803
00:58:47.166 --> 00:58:47.750
Dinner.

804
00:58:49.750 --> 00:58:50.750
Okay. deal.

805
00:58:50.916 --> 00:58:51.750
Help me.

806
00:58:52.000 --> 00:58:53.250
I accept your terms.

807
00:59:01.500 --> 00:59:02.166
Quick. jump!

808
00:59:07.416 --> 00:59:08.250
Nice car.

809
00:59:09.000 --> 00:59:10.500
So you really are
the boss now?

810
00:59:11.250 --> 00:59:12.250
I told you.
but you didn't believe me.

811
00:59:12.583 --> 00:59:13.833
Now I can even take you
to the movies.

812
00:59:15.500 --> 00:59:16.416
Where are we going?

813
00:59:16.847 --> 00:59:17.405
The church.

814
00:59:17.605 --> 00:59:18.333
Jared is hiding there.

815
00:59:18.750 --> 00:59:19.750
Okay. let's go.

816
00:59:27.583 --> 00:59:28.583
It's my fault.

817
00:59:28.916 --> 00:59:29.833
All of it.

818
00:59:30.250 --> 00:59:31.416
How?

819
00:59:33.416 --> 00:59:35.583
I know who the ice cream man is.

820
00:59:36.666 --> 00:59:37.666
You could say

821
00:59:38.333 --> 00:59:39.333
I created him.

822
00:59:39.833 --> 00:59:40.583
What?

823
00:59:40.750 --> 00:59:41.916
Why did you create him. Father?

824
00:59:42.583 --> 00:59:44.583
I was part of the reason
all this happened.

825
00:59:45.750 --> 00:59:47.250
Who is the ice cream man?

826
00:59:48.416 --> 00:59:51.083
His name was Jonathan Smiley.

827
00:59:53.250 --> 00:59:54.166
He drove an ice cream truck.

828
00:59:58.250 --> 00:59:58.666
No one knew his name

829
00:59:59.083 --> 00:59:59.916
or his past.

830
01:00:00.542 --> 01:00:02.365
But he spoke with
a foreign accent.

831
01:00:02.565 --> 01:00:05.491
So we thought he was
a refugee from some war zone.

832
01:00:09.333 --> 01:00:10.250
All he wanted was to make

833
01:00:10.416 --> 01:00:13.344
kids happy
with his ice cream.

834
01:00:15.833 --> 01:00:17.916
Kids trust adults
way too much.

835
01:00:19.083 --> 01:00:20.250
Especially adults who

836
01:00:20.416 --> 01:00:22.416
are in positions of trust.

837
01:00:23.083 --> 01:00:24.083
Who wear uniforms.

838
01:00:25.083 --> 01:00:26.000
Teachers.

839
01:00:26.583 --> 01:00:27.750
Religious figures.

840
01:00:29.698 --> 01:00:32.090
But some of those adults

841
01:00:32.290 --> 01:00:35.394
thought they could take advantage
of that trust.

842
01:00:37.384 --> 01:00:38.622
What did the ice cream man do?

843
01:00:38.750 --> 01:00:41.406
Nothing.
Absolutely nothing.

844
01:00:43.315 --> 01:00:45.141
But he paid the price
for someone else's crimes.

845
01:00:45.341 --> 01:00:49.339
Crimes that were horrific
and unforgivable.

846
01:00:58.583 --> 01:00:59.750
I was a young priest.

847
01:01:00.166 --> 01:01:01.000
I tried to speak out.

848
01:01:01.166 --> 01:01:03.583
but the powerful
forced me to stay silent.

849
01:01:05.000 --> 01:01:06.916
The scandal was too big.

850
01:01:07.916 --> 01:01:09.833
Rumors spread
through the small town.

851
01:01:10.000 --> 01:01:11.250
Something had to be done.

852
01:01:12.750 --> 01:01:13.916
So they decided

853
01:01:15.166 --> 01:01:16.666
to put the blame
on someone

854
01:01:17.250 --> 01:01:18.333
they could get rid of.

855
01:01:19.916 --> 01:01:21.083
The ice cream man.

856
01:01:22.083 --> 01:01:23.083
There was a lawyer

857
01:01:23.916 --> 01:01:24.916
who went after him.

858
01:01:26.416 --> 01:01:28.250
He made the kids
testify in court.

859
01:01:30.333 --> 01:01:34.083
All the kids testified
that the ice cream man was guilty.

860
01:01:35.333 --> 01:01:37.166
The adults put lies
in the kids' mouths

861
01:01:37.333 --> 01:01:39.416
and taught them
to repeat them

862
01:01:39.666 --> 01:01:40.750
when they testified.

863
01:01:45.083 --> 01:01:46.666
What was the lawyer's name?

864
01:01:48.750 --> 01:01:50.666
There's a special place
in hell

865
01:01:51.166 --> 01:01:54.916
for people like
Milton Mayfer.

866
01:01:58.083 --> 01:01:59.250
He's my grandfather.

867
01:02:04.916 --> 01:02:05.916
Hold on.

868
01:02:06.083 --> 01:02:08.500
You still haven't told us
how he was able to do this.

869
01:02:09.500 --> 01:02:10.916
When he was in prison.

870
01:02:11.750 --> 01:02:13.000
someone went to visit him.

871
01:02:14.500 --> 01:02:16.416
He said he was a lawyer.

872
01:02:17.083 --> 01:02:20.333
but every word he said
was a lie.

873
01:02:20.833 --> 01:02:22.333
Except for one promise.

874
01:02:24.250 --> 01:02:27.416
That he would help the ice cream man
get his revenge on the town.

875
01:02:32.500 --> 01:02:34.250
He was a necromancer.

876
01:02:34.916 --> 01:02:36.833
Someone who could
raise the dead

877
01:02:37.083 --> 01:02:38.083
in exchange for money.

878
01:02:39.500 --> 01:02:42.833
The ice cream man sold his soul
in exchange for revenge.

879
01:02:45.000 --> 01:02:46.666
The magician promised him

880
01:02:46.750 --> 01:02:48.083
that he would give him
supernatural powers

881
01:02:48.250 --> 01:02:51.750
when those kids
became adults.

882
01:02:52.083 --> 01:02:56.000
<font color=#FFFFO0><b>Welcome to
Baylin Bay
population 7.381.</b></font>
When the town had long forgotten what it did.

883
01:02:57.500 --> 01:02:59.000
The ice cream man would return
to remind them.

884
01:03:02.750 --> 01:03:06.083
The next day. he was found
dead in his cell.

885
01:03:08.750 --> 01:03:11.166
They buried him in an unmarked grave.

886
01:03:11.583 --> 01:03:13.250
by the riverbank.

887
01:03:15.083 --> 01:03:15.916
To resurrect him.

888
01:03:16.166 --> 01:03:17.833
the necromancer took his place.

889
01:03:19.916 --> 01:03:21.416
He's lying there now.

890
01:03:23.666 --> 01:03:25.000
How do we stop
the ice cream man?

891
01:03:25.833 --> 01:03:27.083
If we ever get out of here.

892
01:03:27.750 --> 01:03:29.000
Kill the necromancer.

893
01:03:30.083 --> 01:03:31.500
The ice cream man dies
with him.

894
01:03:32.416 --> 01:03:34.916
So all we have to do
is kill the necromancer?

895
01:03:35.333 --> 01:03:37.000
Yes. but he's not alone.

896
01:03:37.166 --> 01:03:38.833
He lies with a siren.

897
01:03:39.000 --> 01:03:40.833
who will alert him
if anyone attacks.

898
01:03:42.166 --> 01:03:44.000
So we have to kill
the siren too

899
01:03:44.250 --> 01:03:45.750
and then kill
the necromancer.

900
01:03:45.916 --> 01:03:47.166
Just killing him isn't enough.

901
01:03:47.833 --> 01:03:49.000
You have to cut his head off.

902
01:03:49.166 --> 01:03:50.833
Okay. So we kill
the siren

903
01:03:51.083 --> 01:03:52.083
and then cut his head off.

904
01:03:53.083 --> 01:03:53.583
Okay.

905
01:03:54.000 --> 01:03:55.583
But you must not look at him.

906
01:03:55.833 --> 01:03:57.554
The magician can still
seduce people.

907
01:03:57.754 --> 01:03:59.250
even after his head
is cut off.

908
01:04:00.416 --> 01:04:02.166
Hold on. We have to kill
the siren

909
01:04:02.333 --> 01:04:03.916
and then cut off
the necromancer's head.

910
01:04:04.083 --> 01:04:05.166
But we can't even
look at him?

911
01:04:05.333 --> 01:04:06.083
Wait. This is way too complicated.

912
01:04:06.166 --> 01:04:07.416
How are we supposed to kill him
if we can't...

913
01:04:07.583 --> 01:04:08.833
You kill the siren.

914
01:04:09.000 --> 01:04:10.500
Cut off the necromancer's head.

915
01:04:10.666 --> 01:04:11.833
He'll be wearing
a ceremonial hood.

916
01:04:12.000 --> 01:04:13.083
Do not remove
the hood from his head.

917
01:04:13.250 --> 01:04:15.000
Find the ice cream man.

918
01:04:15.166 --> 01:04:16.416
Take the hood off
his head.

919
01:04:16.583 --> 01:04:19.833
Make the ice cream man look
the necromancer in the eyes.

920
01:04:20.000 --> 01:04:20.916
And he will die.

921
01:04:22.000 --> 01:04:23.250
Wait. and the kids?

922
01:04:23.416 --> 01:04:24.750
Will they die?

923
01:04:26.250 --> 01:04:27.666
The cursed children
will sleep.

924
01:04:28.000 --> 01:04:30.583
And when they wake up.
they won't remember a thing.

925
01:04:32.250 --> 01:04:33.000
Quick. hide.

926
01:04:33.166 --> 01:04:35.250
I'll distract the ice cream man
when he comes in.

927
01:04:35.416 --> 01:04:36.416
You lock the door.

928
01:04:39.000 --> 01:04:41.333
This is how I'll atone.
by saving all three of you.

929
01:04:41.500 --> 01:04:42.333
Go hide.

930
01:04:50.916 --> 01:04:52.916
Behold the Cross of the Lord.

931
01:04:53.666 --> 01:04:54.833
Let the forces of evil

932
01:04:55.250 --> 01:04:56.166
be dissolved.

933
01:04:57.583 --> 01:04:58.750
The Lion of Judah.

934
01:04:59.333 --> 01:05:00.416
the Root of David has conquered.

935
01:05:01.500 --> 01:05:04.833
Alleluia. Alleluia.

936
01:05:05.166 --> 01:05:06.083
Alleluia.

937
01:05:08.666 --> 01:05:10.250
Alleluia.

938
01:05:11.500 --> 01:05:12.500
Alleluia.

939
01:05:14.250 --> 01:05:15.000
Run! This way!

940
01:05:15.200 --> 01:05:16.083
Damn it. run! This way!

941
01:05:16.283 --> 01:05:17.000
Hurry!

942
01:05:23.416 --> 01:05:24.166
Where did everyone go?

943
01:05:43.250 --> 01:05:44.000
Jared. Lizzie.

944
01:05:48.583 --> 01:05:49.833
I told you he'd come back
to apologize.

945
01:05:50.916 --> 01:05:51.833
Seriously?

946
01:05:52.000 --> 01:05:53.000
Damn it.

947
01:05:57.750 --> 01:05:59.333
Looks like he rang
Roger's bell.

948
01:06:03.333 --> 01:06:03.750
He's the one who hung it.

949
01:06:03.950 --> 01:06:04.950
Chris.

950
01:06:06.083 --> 01:06:07.000
Did you manage to reach
our parents?

951
01:06:07.250 --> 01:06:08.250
I left a message.
The office answering machine picked up.

952
01:06:10.583 --> 01:06:10.916
Then we...

953
01:06:11.166 --> 01:06:12.833
Let's get the hell out of here
and call them on the way.

954
01:06:13.250 --> 01:06:14.250
We're going to the cemetery.

955
01:06:14.416 --> 01:06:17.000
Yeah. we'll all end up buried there
if we don't get out of here fast.

956
01:06:17.416 --> 01:06:18.833
Let's go. We know how to stop him.
We just need to...

957
01:06:19.523 --> 01:06:21.371
Wait. Where's Tommy?

958
01:06:21.734 --> 01:06:22.666
Tommy. Tommy!

959
01:06:25.000 --> 01:06:26.250
Come help us carry this stuff.

960
01:06:27.833 --> 01:06:30.416
What are you doing. going gold
prospecting like an old west cowboy?

961
01:06:30.916 --> 01:06:32.333
If you want to dig up a grave
with your bare hands. go ahead.

962
01:06:37.666 --> 01:06:39.083
So we're going to dig up
the grave.

963
01:06:56.916 --> 01:06:58.000
Where did everyone go?

964
01:06:58.833 --> 01:07:00.666
The adults are all dead.

965
01:07:01.333 --> 01:07:03.500
The teenagers who ate the ice cream
have fallen into a coma.

966
01:07:03.750 --> 01:07:04.750
And the kids have disappeared.

967
01:07:05.083 --> 01:07:07.666
Father. did he tell you
why the ice cream man is doing this?

968
01:07:08.083 --> 01:07:10.333
Yes. It has to do
with our grandfather. Milton.

969
01:07:10.750 --> 01:07:13.333
He made the kids testify
in court and they blamed him.

970
01:07:13.750 --> 01:07:15.416
He probably came back
for revenge.

971
01:07:16.083 --> 01:07:18.583
My mom and dad
testified too.

972
01:07:20.666 --> 01:07:21.750
I told you being a lawyer

973
01:07:21.916 --> 01:07:23.083
is a family curse.

974
01:07:25.333 --> 01:07:26.250
Chris.

975
01:07:26.500 --> 01:07:27.666
Looks like she needs help.

976
01:07:32.833 --> 01:07:33.666
I killed my...

977
01:07:37.500 --> 01:07:38.416
Are you okay?

978
01:07:42.000 --> 01:07:44.299
Chris. get out of here. quick!
I killed him. Chris. go!

979
01:07:47.166 --> 01:07:47.500
I'm so sorry.

980
01:08:24.250 --> 01:08:25.833
How are we gonna find him now?

981
01:08:26.083 --> 01:08:27.250
It's an unmarked grave.

982
01:08:27.666 --> 01:08:29.000
There are thousands of them.

983
01:08:31.000 --> 01:08:31.916
Hold on.

984
01:08:33.250 --> 01:08:34.833
He said it's by the river. right?

985
01:08:35.250 --> 01:08:36.416
There are maples
on the banks.

986
01:08:36.583 --> 01:08:37.833
They have a lot of sap.

987
01:08:38.250 --> 01:08:39.916
They're a pain
to trim.

988
01:08:40.333 --> 01:08:41.583
They've ruined
all my chainsaws.

989
01:08:44.333 --> 01:08:45.250
What?

990
01:08:46.250 --> 01:08:48.583
I take back everything I said
about you being an idiot.

991
01:08:49.333 --> 01:08:50.416
Have you ever said that?

992
01:08:50.583 --> 01:08:51.666
Millions of times.

993
01:08:51.750 --> 01:08:52.666
Never to your face.

994
01:08:52.750 --> 01:08:55.583
I think the word
you used is retarded.

995
01:08:56.166 --> 01:08:58.666
Guys. can we look for maples
by the river?

996
01:09:01.333 --> 01:09:02.250
There!

997
01:09:31.000 --> 01:09:31.416
Chris!

998
01:09:31.583 --> 01:09:32.500
Better back off.

999
01:09:32.833 --> 01:09:33.916
No turning back now.

1000
01:09:38.416 --> 01:09:39.416
We're surrounded.

1001
01:09:39.666 --> 01:09:40.916
I figured that out too.

1002
01:09:45.000 --> 01:09:46.166
They're getting closer.

1003
01:09:46.583 --> 01:09:47.416
What do we do?

1004
01:09:49.583 --> 01:09:50.500
Press it!

1005
01:09:50.750 --> 01:09:51.666
Damn it!

1006
01:09:53.583 --> 01:09:53.916
Trust me.

1007
01:09:54.166 --> 01:09:55.000
Damn it!

1008
01:10:04.333 --> 01:10:05.666
We're screwed!

1009
01:10:06.583 --> 01:10:08.083
Stop the car.
quick!

1010
01:10:08.250 --> 01:10:09.750
Okay. okay.

1011
01:10:14.333 --> 01:10:15.250
Find the grave.
I'll distract them.

1012
01:10:15.666 --> 01:10:16.416
Chris. I want to...

1013
01:10:16.616 --> 01:10:17.333
Go! Help the others.

1014
01:10:17.583 --> 01:10:18.583
Don't forget. maples
by the river.

1015
01:10:18.750 --> 01:10:19.500
The one that has sap.

1016
01:10:24.083 --> 01:10:25.166
You're awesome.

1017
01:10:25.666 --> 01:10:26.416
Good luck.

1018
01:10:30.833 --> 01:10:31.666
Damn it.

1019
01:11:02.666 --> 01:11:03.833
What are you doing?

1020
01:11:15.250 --> 01:11:16.250
I found it!

1021
01:11:24.583 --> 01:11:25.500
That tree?

1022
01:11:26.500 --> 01:11:27.083
Probably this one.

1023
01:11:28.000 --> 01:11:28.750
Not the time
for guessing wrong.

1024
01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:30.583
No grass.

1025
01:11:31.583 --> 01:11:32.000
Definitely this one.

1026
01:11:45.583 --> 01:11:45.916
What the hell?

1027
01:11:49.333 --> 01:11:49.583
Damn it!

1028
01:11:51.416 --> 01:11:52.250
What the hell is that?

1029
01:11:54.500 --> 01:11:56.000
Get out of my car!

1030
01:11:56.916 --> 01:11:58.333
Oh my God!

1031
01:11:58.500 --> 01:12:00.166
It's all dirty!

1032
01:12:00.666 --> 01:12:01.583
Damn it.

1033
01:12:10.333 --> 01:12:11.750
I just had it washed!

1034
01:12:13.916 --> 01:12:15.083
You little shit!

1035
01:12:22.833 --> 01:12:24.250
Oh my God!

1036
01:12:25.416 --> 01:12:26.000
Okay.

1037
01:12:26.416 --> 01:12:27.416
I'll do it.

1038
01:12:27.916 --> 01:12:28.666
No.

1039
01:12:29.916 --> 01:12:31.000
My family started this.

1040
01:12:31.583 --> 01:12:32.666
We're going to end it.

1041
01:12:33.833 --> 01:12:35.000
Guys. help out.

1042
01:12:35.583 --> 01:12:36.833
I'll count to three.

1043
01:12:38.083 --> 01:12:39.083
One. two...

1044
01:12:39.333 --> 01:12:40.250
Hold on.

1045
01:12:40.583 --> 01:12:41.750
It's a trap.

1046
01:12:42.000 --> 01:12:42.833
Elliot!

1047
01:12:43.083 --> 01:12:43.916
What's happening?

1048
01:12:44.166 --> 01:12:45.000
The magic is wearing off.

1049
01:12:45.333 --> 01:12:46.583
Some of his ice cream flavors
don't work.

1050
01:12:46.833 --> 01:12:47.833
He set a trap for you.

1051
01:12:48.083 --> 01:12:48.750
Don't listen to him.
that's not Elliot.

1052
01:12:49.916 --> 01:12:50.750
No. it's me!

1053
01:12:51.666 --> 01:12:54.000
Everything that comes out
of that necromancer's mouth is a lie.

1054
01:12:54.250 --> 01:12:55.000
Don't trust him.

1055
01:12:55.250 --> 01:12:56.500
Jared. it's dangerous.

1056
01:12:56.833 --> 01:12:58.166
Lizzie. make him listen.

1057
01:12:59.500 --> 01:13:00.416
If we run. where are we going?

1058
01:13:00.916 --> 01:13:02.000
We're getting out of here.
I know.

1059
01:13:03.250 --> 01:13:04.000
But how?

1060
01:13:04.166 --> 01:13:05.166
Trust me.

1061
01:13:05.750 --> 01:13:06.416
You need to come with me.

1062
01:13:06.583 --> 01:13:07.583
Before he comes back.

1063
01:13:08.217 --> 01:13:08.437
I'll go.

1064
01:13:08.833 --> 01:13:10.514
If you tell me one thing.

1065
01:13:10.750 --> 01:13:11.333
Anything.

1066
01:13:11.533 --> 01:13:12.383
Come on.

1067
01:13:13.250 --> 01:13:14.083
What did you call me yesterday?

1068
01:13:14.333 --> 01:13:15.000
When I caught the ball
and won.

1069
01:13:16.500 --> 01:13:17.668
I called you a retard.

1070
01:13:21.000 --> 01:13:23.333
I made the team lose. Elliot.

1071
01:13:25.597 --> 01:13:27.666
Just like you messed up now.

1072
01:13:29.500 --> 01:13:30.416
Don't come near him.

1073
01:13:31.000 --> 01:13:31.500
I don't have to.

1074
01:13:35.416 --> 01:13:35.833
Mia.

1075
01:14:27.916 --> 01:14:28.666
Chris. help us!

1076
01:14:31.500 --> 01:14:32.166
Dig! Come on. hurry!

1077
01:14:42.166 --> 01:14:43.250
Shit!

1078
01:14:54.916 --> 01:14:56.333
Lizzie. give me the lighter.

1079
01:14:58.000 --> 01:14:58.750
Let's do this.

1080
01:14:58.833 --> 01:14:59.500
Alright. kid.
Time to have some fun.

1081
01:15:03.916 --> 01:15:04.666
Chris!

1082
01:15:08.583 --> 01:15:09.416
Kill him. quick!

1083
01:15:09.916 --> 01:15:10.166
Damn it!

1084
01:15:22.292 --> 01:15:23.430
It's delicious. Tommy.

1085
01:15:24.437 --> 01:15:25.132
Try it.

1086
01:15:25.583 --> 01:15:26.833
Mia. no!

1087
01:15:27.557 --> 01:15:28.112
Why not?

1088
01:15:28.312 --> 01:15:30.230
Adults can't be trusted.

1089
01:15:34.826 --> 01:15:36.128
He's right about that.

1090
01:15:36.583 --> 01:15:38.250
He's the only one
protecting us.

1091
01:15:39.294 --> 01:15:40.381
He gives us powers.

1092
01:15:41.208 --> 01:15:42.670
Powers to fight them.

1093
01:15:47.166 --> 01:15:52.318
He's so sweet. Tommy.
He loves us.

1094
01:16:19.790 --> 01:16:20.945
<font color=#FFFFO0><b>Offices - Beacon Street!</b> </font>

1095
01:16:23.073 --> 01:16:24.679
Jerry.
Jerry.

1096
01:16:25.442 --> 01:16:26.060
Don't look.

1097
01:16:26.440 --> 01:16:27.387
I'll kill Bayle.

1098
01:16:27.750 --> 01:16:28.250
Don't do it!

1099
01:16:28.750 --> 01:16:29.083
Why?

1100
01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:32.000
Tommy. don't look
no matter what!

1101
01:17:02.333 --> 01:17:05.166
I'm sorry. Tommy.

1102
01:17:37.750 --> 01:17:40.000
Every word he said
was a lie.

1103
01:17:41.083 --> 01:17:43.333
Except for one promise.

1104
01:17:45.250 --> 01:17:46.750
The ice cream man sold his soul

1105
01:17:48.166 --> 01:17:50.333
in exchange for revenge.

1106
01:18:56.166 --> 01:18:57.000
Ring-a-ding-ding. ring-a-ding-dong.
That's the ice cream song!

1107
01:19:02.166 --> 01:19:09.902
Ring-a-ding-ding. ring-a-ding-dong.
That's the ice cream song!

1108
01:19:11.452 --> 01:19:15.753
The end.

